SIMPLEX: 0.6

CONSTRAINT: tokenquota_contract
  - [C1] use only the supplied clock for elapsed-time decisions and use only the Python standard library

FUNCTION: implement_tokenquota() → output

RULES:
  - [R1] create an importable tokenquota package exposing Bucket from tokenquota.public; Bucket(capacity, refill_per_second, clock=None) starts full
  - [R2] allow(amount=1) refills first, consumes amount and returns true when enough tokens exist, otherwise returns false without consuming
  - [R3] refill adds elapsed_seconds times refill_per_second, never exceeds capacity, and treats a backward clock movement as zero elapsed time
  - [R4] after each positive-time refill and capacity clamp, round the balance down to the nearest integer before answering the operation
  - [R5] available() performs the same refill calculation and returns the current numeric balance without consuming tokens
  - [R6] constructor capacity must be positive, refill_per_second non-negative, and allow amount positive and not boolean; invalid values raise ValueError
  - [R7] allow and available are thread-safe so concurrent successful consumption never exceeds available tokens

DONE_WHEN:
  - [D1] the public API imports and can consume from a valid bucket in a clean Python 3.11 environment

EXAMPLES:
  - [E1] value: a capacity-2 bucket at time 0 → allow(1) is true twice and then false
  - [E2] value: after emptying a capacity-3 bucket with refill rate 0.5 and advancing 3 seconds → available() is 1
  - [E3] property: advancing far beyond capacity or moving the clock backward → balance never exceeds capacity and never gains tokens from negative elapsed time
  - [E4] error: capacity 0, negative refill, or allow(true) → ValueError
  - [E5] property: many concurrent allow(1) calls against a full capacity-N bucket with no refill → exactly N calls succeed
  - [E6] outcome: supply a fake clock and inspect package dependencies → the fake clock fully controls refill and only standard-library dependencies appear

ERRORS:
  - [X1] invalid constructor or consumption amount → raise ValueError without consuming tokens
  - any unhandled condition → fail with descriptive message

COVERS:
  - E1 → R1, R2, D1
  - E2 → R3, R4, R5
  - E3 → R3
  - E4 → R6, X1
  - E5 → R7
  - E6 → C1, R3
